WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:17.380 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  you know it's a great idea stuffing a  hundred players into a plane to  parachute down on a desolate island to  scavenge for weapons armor and supplies  in hopes of surviving a bloody  deathmatch throwing the impending doom  of an electric field that forces players  into an ever-shrinking warzone and you  get player unknowns battlegrounds this  foreboding gameplay concept results in  an exhilarating multiplayer shooter with  several randomized variables that  challenge you to adapt no one matches  the same and that's what keeps you  coming back for more  despite glaring technical flaws pugsy  emerges as the most accessible  streamlined battle royale game to date  gone are the more granular gameplay  elements of pub G's forebears like  crafting bleeding arduous navigation pub  G is a distilled version of the battle  royale style which makes learning curve  less steep jumping into a match is less  daunting and faster pace than something  like h1z1 king of the kill or earlier  armor mods you're expected to scavenge  for weapons ammo armor and health packs  these critical items litter the city  centres towns and abandoned structures  across the games two different maps  tension and anticipation fill the air  even in an early phase of a match you  have to account for your plane's flight  path and determine if you want to pick a  fight as soon as possible  then it's a race to find the first gun  or immediately throw hands in a  hilariously janky boxing match on the  flipside parachuting to a more distant  town results in a less stressful hunt  for equipment but you won't always get  the gear that you want in squads sharing  an abundance of ammo and health packs or  scouting to relocate highlights the  tactical advantage of team play even in  the opening minutes it's absolutely  necessary to juggle all of these factors  but by the same token this can prove to  be exhausting and repetitive despite  having relatively smooth inventory  management it's demoralizing to spend a  majority of a match gearing up only to  lose in the first firefight or die  unceremoniously from dissing gunfire but  that's the give-and-take you have to  accept in pub g4 the more rewarding  moments to surface  [Music]  [Music]  don't forget you have to face the dread  of the slow yet  ominous blue circle of death that forces  players into an increasingly smaller  zone regardless of the area you land in  the random nature of where the circle  converges within a huge map ensures that  no one matches exactly the same and many  shooters were captures owns and specific  choke points dictate the action pub G  leverages simple variables to stave off  monotony you never really know where the  final firefight will take place or which  position is most advantageous when  things heat up until the blue zone comes  into view positioning scouting and  knowing when to engage are incredibly  important for success  these are tenants that feed into the  emergent tactics formed in a matter of  seconds especially when playing in a  group spotting enemy movement presents  an opening for a kill that could turn  the tide of battle but you also risk  leaving yourself vulnerable pursue the  enemy and brace yourself for bullets  raining down or fire from afar and give  a position away to other players in the  event of getting knocked out teams can  revive you before you bleed out but  they're defenseless as the revived  countdown ticks pub G is a series of  calculated risks it's not entirely new  to video games but the unpredictability  of where and when these moments happen  keeps the game fresh as you inch toward  becoming the last combatant standing  tension ramps up exponentially the  risk/reward nature of pub G is  compounded by the fact that matches  become more of an investment as they go  on but because of how much you have to  work to achieve victory winning is  intrinsically rewarding even without a  tangible prize at the end  that's not to say that the only triumph  comes from winning though survival  itself is an achievement every kill  feels earned and recognizing mistakes in  a heated battle is a lesson learned pub  G retains some of the military  simulation roots of its predecessors and  the game is better for it guns aren't  easy to wield recoil is a major factor  that negates the effectiveness of full  auto firing modes outside of close  quarter encounters bullet drop makes  sniping much more challenging than  simply lining up your crosshairs health  packs take time to be applied which  makes you think twice about healing  under pressure but to experience the  most satisfying parts of pub G you'll  likely go through a lot of trial and  error as of now there aren't any in-game  tutorials to lay out the basics or jump  start newcomers even after several hours  you may still not realize something as  simple as the fact that you can hold the  ctrl key right-click items in the  inventory to drop specific quantities  for your squadmates battlegrounds lacks  technical refinement as well the game is  noticeably improved from its early  access days but frame rates can still  fluctuate inexplicably even a high NPC  can have trouble maintaining a steady  framerate with relatively modest  graphics settings evidence of the game's  ongoing optimisation issues on top of  the in-game performance problems the  fear of seemingly random crashes in  connection difficulties linger if and  when the strike a good match is ruined  the technical shortcomings of player  unknowns battlegrounds can undermine its  broader achievement however pub G  focuses on streamlining the core tenants  that make the genre so enjoyable each  phase of a match presents a different  type of tension its equal parts  thrilling and terrifying all driven by  the insatiable desire to be the last  person or squad standing  whether you play solo or in a group  successfully executing adaptive tactics  makes for an incredibly tense and  rewarding experience every player has  unique stories of their most memorable  matches and even after hundreds of hours  player unknowns battlegrounds keeps on  giving  [Music]  you  [Music]

